    'Sandboxed cross-origin requests.' => 'Permintaan dari iframe lintas-origin yang diberi atribut sandbox.',
    'Some applications might whitelist the [[C0]] origin to support local development of the application. For example, suppose an application receives the following cross-origin request:' => 'Sebagian pengembang mengizinkan origin [[C0]] untuk kebutuhan pengujian lokal, misalnya pada permintaan berikut:',
    'And the server responds with:' => 'Lalu server merespons dengan:',
    'In this situation, an attacker can use various tricks to generate a cross-origin request containing the value [[C0]] in the Origin header. This will satisfy the whitelist, leading to cross-domain access. For example, this can be done using a sandboxed [[C1]] cross-origin request of the form:' => 'Penyerang dapat membangkitkan permintaan ber-Origin [[C0]] dengan membungkus skrip eksploitasi di dalam tag [[C1]] bersandbox seperti berikut:',
    'Even "correctly" configured CORS establishes a trust relationship between two origins. If a website trusts an origin that is vulnerable to cross-site scripting (XSS), then an attacker could exploit the XSS to inject some JavaScript that uses CORS to retrieve sensitive information from the site that trusts the vulnerable application.' => 'Bahkan jika whitelist CORS dikonfigurasi ketat, mempercayai satu origin subdomain yang memiliki celah XSS tetap memungkinkan penyerang membaca data sensitif situs induk lewat CORS.',
