    'The attacker intercepts the plain HTTP request, and returns a spoofed response containing a CORS request to:' => 'Penyerang mencegat permintaan HTTP itu lalu membalas dengan halaman palsu berisi skrip CORS ke:',
    'The victim\'s browser makes the CORS request, including the origin:' => 'Browser korban mengirim permintaan CORS dengan origin:',
    'The application allows the request because this is a [[S0]]whitelisted[[/S0]] origin. The requested sensitive data is returned in the response.' => 'Aplikasi mengizinkannya karena origin ada di [[S0]]whitelist[[/S0]] dan mengirim kembali data sensitif.',
    'The attacker\'s spoofed page can read the sensitive data and transmit it to any domain under the attacker\'s control.' => 'Skrip pada halaman palsu membaca data tersebut dan meneruskannya ke server penyerang.',
    'This attack is effective even if the vulnerable website is otherwise robust in its usage of HTTPS, with no HTTP endpoint and all cookies flagged as secure.' => 'Serangan ini tetap berhasil meski situs utama memakai HTTPS penuh dan seluruh cookienya bertanda Secure.',
    'Most CORS attacks rely on the presence of the response header:' => 'Sebagian besar eksploitasi CORS membutuhkan header respons berikut:',
    'Without that header, the victim user\'s browser will refuse to send their cookies, meaning the attacker will only gain access to unauthenticated content, which they could just as easily access by browsing directly to the target website.' => 'Tanpa header tersebut, browser tidak mengirimkan cookie sesi sehingga penyerang hanya bisa mengakses data publik.',
    'However, there is one common situation where an attacker can\'t access a website directly: when it\'s part of an organization\'s intranet, and located within private IP address space. Internal websites are often held to a lower security standard than external sites, enabling attackers to find vulnerabilities and gain further access. For example, a cross-origin request within a private network may be as follows:' => 'Namun pengecualian krusial berlaku untuk aplikasi intranet di jaringan IP privat yang tidak dapat dijangkau langsung dari internet:',
    'The application server is trusting resource requests from any origin without credentials. If users within the private IP address space access the public internet then a CORS-based attack can be performed from the external site that uses the victim\'s browser as a proxy for accessing intranet resources.' => 'Bila aplikasi internal memakai wildcard tanpa autentikasi cookie dan pegawai perusahaan membuka situs eksternal penyerang, browser korban berperan sebagai proxy untuk membaca data intranet.',
    'How to prevent CORS-based attacks' => 'Cara mencegah serangan berbasis CORS',
    'CORS vulnerabilities arise primarily as misconfigurations. Prevention is therefore a configuration problem. The following sections describe some effective defenses against CORS attacks.' => 'Kerentanan CORS umumnya bersumber dari kesalahan konfigurasi. Langkah pencegahan utama meliputi:',
    'Proper configuration of cross-origin requests' => 'Konfigurasi yang tepat untuk permintaan lintas-origin',
    'If a web resource contains sensitive information, the origin should be properly specified in the [[C0]] header.' => 'Jika resource memuat data sensitif, tentukan origin yang diizinkan secara spesifik dan akurat pada header [[C0]].',
    'Only allow trusted sites' => 'Hanya izinkan situs yang benar-benar tepercaya',
    'It may seem obvious but origins specified in the [[C0]] header should only be sites that are trusted. In particular, dynamically reflecting origins from cross-origin requests without validation is readily exploitable and should be avoided.' => 'Pastikan hanya domain tepercaya yang tercantum di [[C0]]. Jangan pernah memantulkan header Origin secara dinamis tanpa validasi persis terhadap whitelist.',
    'Avoid whitelisting null' => 'Hindari mengizinkan nilai origin null',
    'Avoid using the header [[C0]]. Cross-origin resource calls from internal documents and sandboxed requests can specify the [[C1]] origin. CORS headers should be properly defined in respect of trusted origins for private and public servers.' => 'Hindari konfigurasi [[C0]] karena dokumen lokal maupun iframe bersandbox dapat memalsukan origin [[C1]].',
    'Avoid wildcards in internal networks' => 'Hindari wildcard di jaringan internal',
    'Avoid using wildcards in internal networks. Trusting network configuration alone to protect internal resources is not sufficient when internal browsers can access untrusted external domains.' => 'Jangan mengandalkan isolasi jaringan semata sambil memasang wildcard di intranet, karena browser pengguna di jaringan internal masih terhubung ke internet.',
    'CORS is not a substitute for server-side security policies' => 'CORS bukan pengganti kontrol keamanan di sisi server',
    'CORS defines browser behaviors and is never a replacement for server-side protection of sensitive data - an attacker can directly forge a request from any trusted origin. Therefore, web servers should continue to apply protections over sensitive data, such as authentication and session management, in addition to properly configured CORS.' => 'CORS hanya membatasi perilaku browser, bukan akses langsung lewat curl atau proksi yang bisa memalsukan header Origin apa saja. Autentikasi dan otorisasi sisi server wajib tetap ditegakkan.',
    'Find CORS vulnerabilities using Burp Suite\'s web vulnerability scanner' => 'Menemukan kerentanan CORS dengan pemindai kerentanan web',

    // same-origin-policy
    'In this section we explain what the same-origin policy (SOP) is and how it is implemented.' => 'Bagian ini menjelaskan apa itu same-origin policy (SOP) dan bagaimana browser menerapkannya.',
    'What is the same-origin policy?' => 'Apa itu same-origin policy?',
    'The same-origin policy is a web browser security mechanism that aims to prevent websites from attacking each other.' => 'Same-origin policy adalah mekanisme keamanan inti pada browser web untuk mencegah satu situs menyerang atau mencuri data situs lain.',
    'The same-origin policy restricts scripts on one origin from accessing data from another origin. An origin consists of a URI scheme, domain and port number. For example, consider the following URL:' => 'SOP membatasi skrip di satu origin agar tidak bisa membaca data dari origin lain. Suatu origin didefinisikan dari kombinasi skema URI, domain, dan nomor port. Contohnya URL berikut:',
    'This uses the scheme [[C0]], the domain [[C1]], and the port number [[C2]]. The following table shows how the same-origin policy will be applied if content at the above URL tries to access other origins:' => 'URL ini memakai skema [[C0]], domain [[C1]], dan port bawaan [[C2]]. Tabel berikut menunjukkan bagaimana SOP menilai akses ke origin lain:',
    'URL accessed' => 'URL yang diakses',
    'Access permitted?' => 'Akses diizinkan?',
    'Yes: same scheme, domain, and port' => 'Ya: skema, domain, dan port sama',
    'No: different scheme and port' => 'Tidak: skema dan port berbeda',
    'No: different domain' => 'Tidak: domain berbeda',
    'No: different port*' => 'Tidak: port berbeda*',
    '*Internet Explorer will allow this access because IE does not take account of the port number when applying the same-origin policy.' => '*Internet Explorer lama mengizinkan akses ini karena mengabaikan nomor port saat mengecek same-origin policy.',
    'When a browser sends an HTTP request from one origin to another, any cookies, including authentication session cookies, relevant to the other domain are also sent as part of the request. This means that the response will be generated within the user\'s session, and include any relevant data that is specific to the user. Without the same-origin policy, if you visited a malicious website, it would be able to read your emails from GMail, private messages from Facebook, etc.' => 'Saat browser mengirim permintaan lintas situs, cookie milik situs tujuan otomatis ikut terkirim sehingga respons yang terbentuk berisi data pribadi korban. Tanpa SOP, situs berbahaya mana pun bisa langsung membaca isi kotak masuk email atau akun bank Anda yang sedang login.',
    'The same-origin policy generally controls the access that JavaScript code has to content that is loaded cross-domain. Cross-origin loading of page resources is generally permitted. For example, the SOP allows embedding of images via the [[C0]] tag, media via the [[C1]] tag, and JavaScript via the [[C2]] tag. However, while these external resources can be loaded by the page, any JavaScript on the page won\'t be able to read the contents of these resources.' => 'SOP umumnya mengizinkan pemuatan resource lintas domain lewat tag [[C0]], [[C1]], maupun [[C2]], tetapi melarang skrip halaman membaca mentah isi teks atau data dari resource lintas origin tersebut.',
    'There are various exceptions to the same-origin policy:' => 'Beberapa pengecualian resmi pada same-origin policy meliputi:',
    'Some objects are writable but not readable cross-domain, such as the [[C0]] object or the [[C1]] property from iframes or new windows.' => 'Objek tertentu dapat ditulis namun tidak dapat dibaca lintas domain, seperti [[C0]] atau [[C1]].',
    'Some objects are readable but not writable cross-domain, such as the [[C0]] property of the [[C1]] object (which stores the number of frames being used on the page) and the [[C2]] property.' => 'Objek tertentu dapat dibaca namun tidak bisa dimodifikasi, misalnya properti [[C0]] pada [[C1]] serta [[C2]].',
    'The [[C0]] function can generally be called cross-domain on the [[C1]] object.' => 'Fungsi [[C0]] umumnya tetap bisa dipanggil lintas domain pada objek [[C1]].',
    'You can call certain functions cross-domain. For example, you can call the functions [[C0]], [[C1]] and [[C2]] on a new window. The [[C3]] function can also be called on iframes and new windows in order to send messages from one domain to another.' => 'Fungsi tertentu seperti [[C0]], [[C1]], dan [[C2]] dapat dipanggil pada jendela terpisah, serta fungsi [[C3]] untuk mengirim pesan antar-origin secara terstruktur.',
    'Due to legacy requirements, the same-origin policy is more relaxed when dealing with cookies, so they are often accessible from all subdomains of a site even though each subdomain is technically a different origin. You can partially mitigate this risk using the [[C0]] cookie flag.' => 'Karena alasan kompatibilitas lama, aturan cakupan cookie lebih longgar antar subdomain dibanding SOP pada DOM. Risiko akses cookie oleh skrip tetap perlu dibatasi dengan flag [[C0]].',
    'Why is the same-origin policy necessary?' => 'Mengapa same-origin policy diperlukan?',
    'How is the same-origin policy implemented?' => 'Bagaimana same-origin policy diterapkan?',
    'It\'s possible to relax same-origin policy using [[C0]]. This special property allows you to relax SOP for a specific domain, but only if it\'s part of your FQDN (fully qualified domain name). For example, you might have a domain [[C1]] and you would like to read the contents of that domain on [[C2]]. To do so, both domains need to set [[C3]] to [[C4]]. Then SOP will allow access between the two domains despite their different origins. In the past it was possible to set [[C5]] to a TLD such as [[C6]], which allowed access between any domains on the same TLD, but now modern browsers prevent this.' => 'Anda dapat melonggarkan same-origin policy menggunakan [[C0]] agar dua subdomain di bawah FQDN yang sama (misalnya [[C1]] dan [[C2]]) dapat saling membaca konten dengan mengatur [[C3]] ke [[C4]]. Dahulu properti [[C5]] bahkan bisa disetel ke TLD seperti [[C6]] sehingga semua domain pada TLD yang sama bisa saling mengakses, tetapi browser modern kini memblokir hal tersebut.',

    // access-control-allow-origin
    'CORS and the Access-Control-Allow-Origin response header' => 'CORS dan header respons Access-Control-Allow-Origin',
    'In this section we explain what the [[C0]] header is in respect of CORS, and how it forms part of CORS implementation.' => 'Bagian ini membahas fungsi header [[C0]] dalam protokol CORS dan bagaimana header tersebut bekerja.',
    'The [[A0]]cross-origin resource sharing[[/A0]] specification provides controlled relaxation of the [[A1]]same-origin policy[[/A1]] for HTTP requests to one website domain from another through the use of a collection of HTTP headers. Browsers permit access to responses to cross-origin requests based upon these header instructions.' => 'Spesifikasi [[A0]]CORS[[/A0]] melonggarkan [[A1]]same-origin policy[[/A1]] secara terkontrol melalui pertukaran header HTTP antara server dan browser.',
    'What is the Access-Control-Allow-Origin response header?' => 'Apa itu header respons Access-Control-Allow-Origin?',
    'The [[C0]] header is included in the response from one website to a request originating from another website, and identifies the permitted origin of the request. A web browser compares the Access-Control-Allow-Origin with the requesting website\'s origin and permits access to the response if they match.' => 'Header [[C0]] dikirim server untuk menyebutkan origin mana yang diizinkan membaca respons; browser mencocokkan nilai tersebut dengan origin peminta sebelum membuka akses respons.',
    'Implementing simple cross-origin resource sharing' => 'Menerapkan cross-origin resource sharing sederhana',
    'The cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) specification prescribes header content exchanged between web servers and browsers that restricts origins for web resource requests outside of the origin domain. The CORS specification identifies a collection of protocol headers of which [[C0]] is the most significant. This header is returned by a server when a website requests a cross-domain resource, with an [[C1]] header added by the browser.' => 'Dalam alur sederhana CORS, browser mengirim header [[C1]] bersama permintaan lintas domain, lalu server membalas dengan header [[C0]] untuk mengizinkan origin pengakses.',
    'For example, suppose a website with origin [[C0]] causes the following cross-domain request:' => 'Sebagai contoh, jika situs dari [[C0]] mengirim permintaan lintas domain berikut:',
    'The server on [[C0]] returns the following response:' => 'Server [[C0]] membalas dengan header:',
    'The browser will allow code running on [[C0]] to access the response because the origins match.' => 'Browser pun mengizinkan skrip di [[C0]] membaca respons karena nilainya cocok persis.',
