    'Handling cross-origin resource requests with credentials' => 'Menangani permintaan lintas-origin dengan kredensial',
    'The default behavior of cross-origin resource requests is for requests to be passed without credentials like cookies and the Authorization header. However, the cross-domain server can permit reading of the response when credentials are passed to it by setting the CORS [[C0]] header to true. Now if the requesting website uses JavaScript to declare that it is sending cookies with the request:' => 'Secara default permintaan lintas-origin tidak membawa cookie atau header Authorization. Untuk mengizinkan pembacaan respons berautentikasi, server harus menyetel [[C0]] bernilai true:',
    'And the response to the request is:' => 'Lalu server memberikan respons berikut:',
    'Then the browser will permit the requesting website to read the response, because the [[C0]] response header is set to [[C1]]. Otherwise, the browser will not allow access to the response.' => 'Skrip hanya dapat membaca isi respons apabila header [[C0]] bernilai [[C1]] dan origin cocok spesifik.',
    'Relaxation of CORS specifications with wildcards' => 'Pelonggaran spesifikasi CORS menggunakan wildcard',
